==Trivia==
*His Japanese name, Buchigoma-sama (ブチゴマさま), is derived from 打ち ''buchi'' meaning "hit" or "strike", or 斑, meaning "spots", particularly in the coat of animal, and ゴマさま ''Goma-sama'', [[Sir Seal]]'s Japanese name. It may also involve ''buchikorosu'' (打ち殺す), meaning to "kill cruelly", or ''buchikowasu'' (打ち壊す), meaning "to wreck, mar or spoil".
*According to his Japanese description, the "uncanny world" Zir Zeal came from is the afterlife. あの世 ''ano yo'' ("that world") is a common euphemism for the world after death.
*He is tied with [[Znache]] for the longest burrow distance, at 1,500.

